        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5 \\cot{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\csc^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{2 \\cot^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 \\cot^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 5$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- 16 \\cot{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\csc^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{5 \\cot{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\csc^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{2 \\cot^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{5}{16}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{5}{16}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{5}{16}\\left(\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{5}{16}\\left(\\ln\\left|2 \\cot^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 5\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$",
