        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{- 6 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{3 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=24 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{- 6 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{3 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\ln\\left|3 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 2\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
