      "question": {
        ":question/id": "afc505b2-eb23-556b-b4bb-186a13d68208",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{24}} \\frac{- 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{4 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=4 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 3$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=32 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=3\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{24}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{13}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{24}} \\frac{- 4 \\tan{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)}}{4 \\tan^{2}{\\left(4 x \\right)} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\int_{3}^{\\frac{13}{3}} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth new bounds are positive, so absolute values may be omitted. Evaluate:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{3}^{\\frac{13}{3}}\\right)=- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{13}{3}\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nUsing $\\ln A-\\ln B=\\ln(A/B)$ gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{13}{9}\\right)\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "6ad6f867-c4de-57ca-867b-905db4c575e7",
