      "question": {
        ":question/id": "046e63fb-5a4e-50f5-a8d9-2f71bedde598",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\frac{- 7 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=4 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=3 + 4 \\sqrt{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\frac{- 7 \\tan{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4 \\sec{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{7}{8}\\left(\\int_{3 + 4 \\sqrt{2}}^{11} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth new bounds are positive, so absolute values may be omitted. Evaluate:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7}{8}\\left(\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{3 + 4 \\sqrt{2}}^{11}\\right)=- \\frac{7}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(11\\right)-\\ln\\left(3 + 4 \\sqrt{2}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nUsing $\\ln A-\\ln B=\\ln(A/B)$ gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{7}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{11}{3 + 4 \\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
