      "question": {
        ":question/id": "1892def1-facb-5b2a-adbe-376640d37b4e",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\frac{- 5 \\sin{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\cos{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=40 \\sin{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\cos{\\left(5 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=5\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{10}&\\Longrightarrow u=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\frac{- 5 \\sin{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\cos{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\int_{5}^{9} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth new bounds are positive, so absolute values may be omitted. Evaluate:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{5}^{9}\\right)=- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(9\\right)-\\ln\\left(5\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nUsing $\\ln A-\\ln B=\\ln(A/B)$ gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{9}{5}\\right)\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "1e9873d4-75e4-5c47-9787-4995cb8c94fb",
