      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ef1173f3-df57-500d-84bc-a6ebe384b05c",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{30}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\frac{3 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{\\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- 5 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe negative derivative is included in the factor outside the new integral.\n\nChange both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi}{30}&\\Longrightarrow u=7\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{10}&\\Longrightarrow u=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed bounds decrease; keep their order when subtracting endpoint values.\n\nSubstituting, including the required constant factor, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{30}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{10}} \\frac{3 \\cot{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{\\csc{\\left(5 x \\right)} + 5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\int_{7}^{6} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth new bounds are positive, so absolute values may be omitted. Evaluate:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\left[\\ln u\\right]_{7}^{6}\\right)=- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\ln\\left(6\\right)-\\ln\\left(7\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nUsing $\\ln A-\\ln B=\\ln(A/B)$ gives\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3}{5}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
